# Release & Versioning (SemVer + Changelog + GitHub Releases)

## 1) Versioning standard: SemVer
- Use Semantic Versioning: `MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`.
- Bump rules:
  - MAJOR: backward-incompatible changes
  - MINOR: backward-compatible features
  - PATCH: backward-compatible bug fixes
- Never modify already published releases; fix forward with a new version.

## 2) Tags and release naming
- Git tag format: `vX.Y.Z` (e.g., `v0.3.1`).
- GitHub Release title should match the tag (`vX.Y.Z`).
- Pre-releases use SemVer pre-release syntax (`v1.2.0-rc.1`).

## 3) Changelog policy (Keep a Changelog)
- Maintain a human-readable `CHANGELOG.md`.
- Use Keep a Changelog structure with:
  - `## [Unreleased]`
  - per-release sections ordered chronologically
  - categories like Added/Changed/Deprecated/Removed/Fixed/Security
- Every user-facing change must appear in the changelog (or be explicitly marked "internal/no user impact").

## 4) Release workflow (GitHub Actions)
Choose ONE approach (don’t mix both without ADR):

### A) Tag-driven release (manual version bump, automated GitHub Release)
- Developer updates version + changelog, merges to main, then tags `vX.Y.Z`.
- CI on tag push creates a GitHub Release and attaches release notes:
  - Either use GitHub “auto-generated release notes”
  - Or use a release action to publish release with a prepared body

### B) Automated semantic releases (conventional commits -> auto bump + notes)
- CI derives next version from commit messages, generates notes/changelog, creates tag and GitHub Release automatically.
- Requires strict commit convention and tooling; document it clearly.

## 5) Release notes rules
- Release notes must include:
  - highlights (top 3–7 items)
  - breaking changes (if any) with migration notes
  - links to issues/PRs where possible
- Keep notes concise; do not paste large verbatim content from external sources.

## 6) Definition of "done" for a release PR
- Version updated in the canonical place (project standard)
- `CHANGELOG.md` updated with relevant entries
- CI green
- Tag/release created following the chosen approach
